  "body": "Found during #2176 (PR #2179).\n\n## What happens\n\n`HolderProfile::enclose` (`crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs`) sets the judged `shank_d` from `reach_over(flute_len, shank_top)`. `reach_over` uses inclusive bounds (`b.above <= hi && b.above + b.len >= lo`). Thus a holder band that starts exactly at the shank top widens the full judged shank to the band radius.\n\nExample: the catalog tool `EM-0400-2FL` (Ø12 shank) with a drawn cone holder from r 10 to r 30 at the shank top. The judged `shank_d` is 60 mm. The shank laws then sweep a Ø60 shank from the flute top to the holder foot.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe result is conservative, so it is not a gouge. But it can refuse a legal program: a shank law can report a collision that the real Ø12 shank does not make.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Must the bound be exclusive at the shank top, or must only the band part below the shank top count?\n- Which tests pin the current widening on purpose (#368, #828)?\n\nDone means: a test pins that a band that only touches the shank top does not widen the judged shank, and no collision law reads a smaller body than the real one.\n\nThis is under the safety floor (a collision check), so it is `effort:high`.\n",
